{"id":27964,"slug":"the-uninvited","title":"The Uninvited","year":1944,"country":"United States","duration":99,"spine":677,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/27964-the-uninvited","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/9a47380e81bad08a322032a14158be83/8ftdZ1FybsRNtjEkE0lr8zYDcdx8lQ_large.jpg","description":"A pair of siblings from London (Ray Milland and Ruth Hussey) purchase a surprisingly affordable, lonely cliff-top house in Cornwall, only to discover that it actually carries a ghostly price—and soon they’re caught up in a bizarre romantic triangle from beyond the grave. Rich in atmosphere, The Uninvited, directed by Lewis Allen, was groundbreaking for the seriousness with which it treated the haunted-house genre, and it remains an elegant and eerie experience, featuring a classic score by Victor Young. A tragic family past, a mysteriously locked room, cold chills, bumps in the night—this gothic Hollywood classic has it all. ","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Lewis Allen","slug":"lewis-allen"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Ray Milland","role":"Roderick Fitzgerald","slug":"ray-milland"},{"actor":"Ruth Hussey","role":"Pamela Fitzgerald","slug":"ruth-hussey"},{"actor":"Donald Crisp","role":"Commander Beech","slug":"donald-crisp"},{"actor":"Cornelia Otis Skinner","role":"Miss Holloway","slug":"cornelia-otis-skinner"},{"actor":"Dorothy Stickney","role":"Miss Bird","slug":"dorothy-stickney"},{"actor":"Barbara Everest","role":"Lizzie Flynn","slug":"barbara-everest"},{"actor":"Alan Napier","role":"Dr. Scott","slug":"alan-napier"},{"actor":"Gail Russell","role":"Stella Meredith","slug":"gail-russell"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Lewis Allen","slug":"lewis-allen"},{"role":"Associate producer","person":"Charles Brackett","slug":null},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Dodie Smith","slug":null},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Frank Partos","slug":null},{"role":"Based on the novel by","person":"Dorothy Macardle","slug":null},{"role":"Director